@baseUrl = https://license.example.invalid
@organizationId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@eventId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@ruleId = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
@token = replace-with-delegated-api-token

### Standardized operational events (ViewInventory + ViewFindings)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/organizations/{{organizationId}}/operational-events?limit=100
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Passive connector health, latency, retries and dead-letter totals
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/organizations/{{organizationId}}/connectors/health
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Explicit ticket creation (202 + Location); repeated event/channel requests are deduplicated
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/organizations/{{organizationId}}/operational-events/{{eventId}}/ticket
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "channel": "jira"
}

### Opt in to automatic Jira creation for future selected events (ManagePolicies)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/organizations/{{organizationId}}/notification-rules/{{ruleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ruleId": "{{ruleId}}",
  "name": "Approved high-severity operational tickets",
  "enabled": true,
  "minimumSeverity": 3,
  "findings": false,
  "effectiveAccess": false,
  "added": false,
  "removed": false,
  "changed": false,
  "channel": "jira",
  "connectorKind": "Jira",
  "allowAutomaticTickets": true,
  "eventTypes": ["finding.created", "review.overdue", "scan.failed"]
}

### Invalid event page size (400); unknown event ticket requests return 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/organizations/{{organizationId}}/operational-events?limit=501
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
